# Trivy findings accepted with a documented reason. Keep this list short and
# justified — an unexplained entry here is how a real finding gets buried.

# DS-0002 — "Image user should not be 'root'".
# The image intentionally has no final USER instruction: the container must
# start as root to chown the Home Assistant-managed /data volume (whose
# ownership we don't control), and docker-entrypoint.sh then runs EVERY
# long-running process (gunicorn, the MCP server, provisioning, discovery) as
# the unprivileged `app` user via gosu — see RUN_AS there. Only the supervising
# shell stays root. Same model as the myMeal/Edibl add-ons.
DS-0002
